<title>JAPAN: Hankyu Dept plans big shopping complex.</title>
<headline>Hankyu Dept plans big shopping complex.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hankyu Department Stores Inc said on Thursday it is planning to open a new shopping complex in Sakai, near Osaka, in 2001.</p>
<p>The complex, which will be built by Nippon Steel Corp, will house a branch of Hankyu as well as specialty stores, restaurants and entertainment facilities, the two firms said in a statement.</p>
<p>The complex will have a commercial area of 90,000 sq metres and is expected to open in 2001, they said.</p>
<p>The complex is part of a re-development project by Nippon Steel.</p>
</text>
